#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""rexbar: a status bar for a Rex tab, in a thin pane along its bottom.

  rexbar run    --session S [--window W] [--fit] [--fit-rows N]
  rexbar once   --session S [--width N] [--rows N] [--no-color]
  rexbar open   --session S --window W [--block B]
  rexbar close  --session S --window W [--block B]
  rexbar toggle --session S --window W [--block B]
  rexbar fit    --session S --window W [--block B]

The bar shows, left to right: the ticket (or "scratch"), done/total goals, a
blocked marker and the deepest `doing` goal; a history strip of coloured cells
(pictures, goal status changes, reviews, promote, land), newest at the right;
the session's agents by state; plan usage (5-hour, weekly) and the main agent's
model and context when rexboard has them.

`run` and `once` only read the session, except `<session dir>/bar/`, where the
bar keeps objectives-log.json (goal and review changes it has seen). `open`,
`close`, `toggle` and `fit` print one line of JSON.

--session must be a Rex session id (hex and dashes, optional "session:").
Without --session, $REX_SESSION is used only if Rex knows that session.
"""
